  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&#x2019;s development programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Savisthri is a women-led organisation which has been working since 1994 to build up a people&#x2019;s movement by forming poor and marginalised women in rural and coastal areas of six districts (Galle, Matara, Matale, Anuradhapura, Monaragala and Nuwara Eliya) into small groups, and networking the groups at district and national levels.  Since 2009 a seventh district has been added: Batticaloa.  Group members are resourced and encouraged to improve their families&apos; quality of life through savings schemes and credit unions; ecological home gardening and small business projects; and alternative marketing (selling the produce of their gardens and craftwork in periodic fairs at local and national level).  They are also encouraged to become active and engaged citizens, campaigning and lobbying for people-friendly policy decisions.  Special emphasis is always placed on improved family nutrition and environmental sustainability.  Savisthri has a proven capacity to mobilise its grassroots membership and networks to understand and support district- and national-level campaigns on issues such as food sovereignty, in conjunction with CAFOD partners MONLAR and NAFSO and other like-minded organisations.  In 2011 Savisthri began a process of transforming itself into a women&#x2019;s movement by encouraging its various base groups, credit unions and campaigning committees in each locality to unite as all-purpose community-based organisations, and by handing over decision-making to the District Women&#x2019;s Collectives (DWCs) made up of representatives elected by the membership.  A new initiative planned for 2016 is to train women leaders to engage with local government at Pradeshaya Sabha level, both as citizens and - from 2017 - by putting themselves forward for election.</narrative>
  </description>
